# NOTE on *.mp3 — deliberately NOT blanket-ignored any more.
#
# It used to be, and that caused a real bug: apps/desktop/public/featured-podcast.json
# is tracked and referenced `audioFile: "Study_Studio_Podcast.mp3"`, but the audio
# itself was ignored — so the featured podcast shipped a dangling reference and
# played no audio on any fresh clone. A tracked file must never point at an ignored
# one. Ignore media per-directory instead, so the coupling stays visible.

# Local demo media. Kept on disk (so a developer who has it keeps it) but not
# committed and not shipped: everything under public/ is copied into out/ and into
# the installer, and this file alone was ~65% of that payload.
apps/desktop/assets/

# Local agent/tooling state. Not part of the product, never meant to be committed.
.claude/
.workbuddy-ai/

# A separate project that happens to sit inside this working tree. It has its own
# .git/, .github/ and CLAUDE.md, and 74k+ files. Ignored rather than tracked so it
# cannot be swept into a commit or destroyed by `git clean -fdx` surprises.
# Decide its long-term home separately: sibling repo, or submodule.
deepseek-harness/
